{
  "_contract_version": 1,
  "_description": "ADDITIVE fixture (R2). GET /api/refs/kinds (authenticated, like /api/refs/search): the kinds THIS server resolves, derived from ONE table on the server, so that a client offers only those and draws them without a list of its own. Response 200: {contract_version, kinds[]}, in display order. Each entry: kind (the name in #kind:id); class ('data': cited with '#', read or discussed; 'actor': invocable, cited with '@' — persona and skill; the server only fixes the class here, invoking one is another feature); sigil ('#' or '@', follows from class); id_format ('uuid' = hyphenated UUID, 'project_commit' = <project uuid>:<40 or 64 hex>, 'project_path' = <project uuid>:<path relative to the project root>, 'url' = a normalized http/https address, see kind_ids.json); sensitive (file and commit: GET /api/refs/search suggests them only when project_id or workspace_slug is given, and a chat session reads them only inside a project or workspace it is attached to); label_source (what the label is made of: title, title_or_first_line, first_line, name, title_or_version, path, host); searchable (false for link: nothing to list, it is pasted); open_route (where the app opens it, relative to /workspace/:slug/; {id} is the reference id, {slug} the slug of the result's `project`; null = no page of its own); opens_external (a link opens outside the app); icon (a key to map to an icon). A server that predates this route answers 404 (or the SPA fallback, which is not JSON with a kinds array): the client then offers fallback_kinds, the five kinds of the first release, and sends nothing else. A kind name or a field value the client does not know must be ignored, not offered. GET /api/refs/search without `kinds` still asks for the five fallback kinds; any other kind (for '@': kinds=persona,skill) must be requested by name. Results are ranked by relevance (see search_response.json).",
